From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Telesphoreo <me@telesphoreo.me>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 00:55:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Bound vehicle collision processing

Push and pickup limits do not bound the earlier movement collision query.
A pile of 376 minecarts could still cause 141,000 collision checks per
movement pass, including vehicle events, before logging the push limit.

Bound both movement collision sinks before predicates, events and shapes.
Share separate movement and push/pickup budgets across each world tick.
Cap each phase at the configured limit or 16 raw candidates, and at 256
chunk, section and entity visits. Count nonintersecting entities too.
Keep block collisions and skip excess contacts.

Cancel new minecart spawns when the destination chunk already has 100.
Maintain a counter through existing chunk add/remove operations, with no
age tracking or per-tick scans. Do not remove carts or cargo. Leave saved
piles, movement and dimension transfers alone. Keep warnings infrequent.

